{"term":"шалава","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"shalava","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A sexually promiscuous or loose woman; used as a harsh insult meaning slut or cheap prostitute in criminal argot and broad colloquial speech.","english_term":"slut","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Crossed from феня into general colloquial use; one of the most widely deployed Russian female-targeted sexual insults."}
{"term":"кобыла","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"kobyla","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'mare'; criminal argot for a large, coarse, or sexually available woman — dehumanizes by equine comparison.","english_term":"slut","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The horse metaphor implies both sexual availability and physical coarseness; in prison slang sometimes denotes a female inmate used as a sexual object by others."}
{"term":"сучара","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"suchara","category":"insults","subcategory":"bitch","concept":"bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Intensified augmentative of сука (bitch); a maximally contemptuous insult for a vile or despicable woman.","english_term":"total bitch","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The -ара suffix is a pejorative intensifier; considerably stronger than сука alone; common in criminal argot and street speech."}
{"term":"курва","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"kurva","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A whore or sexually promiscuous woman; a strong insult borrowed from Polish/Ukrainian kurwa.","english_term":"whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Loanword from Polish/Ukrainian; the foreign phonology can intensify its offensive edge in Russian; widely understood and used in Russian criminal speech."}
{"term":"паскуда","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"paskuda","category":"insults","subcategory":"moral_degrade","concept":"wanton_behavior","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A vile, morally depraved, or nasty person; in criminal argot directed at women, implies sexual and moral corruption combined.","english_term":"degenerate","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Less specifically sexual than шалава; the sexual insult dimension emerges primarily from gendered application and context; also used for treacherous male figures."}
{"term":"шкура","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"shkura","category":"insults","subcategory":"prostitute_slur","concept":"sex_worker_archaic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":82,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":83,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hide/pelt/skin'; criminal argot for a sexually available woman or prostitute who sells herself.","english_term":"whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Dual meaning in феня: prostitute or sexually available woman AND informer/snitch — context determines which reading applies; both usages frame the person as something disposable."}
{"term":"телка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"telka","category":"insults","subcategory":"objectifying_term_woman","concept":"wench","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A girl or young woman (crude); literally 'heifer' (young female bovine); objectifying and mildly contemptuous but extremely widespread.","english_term":"chick","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Simplified spelling of тёлка (without ё); occupies a register similar to English 'chick' or British 'bird'; crude but not maximally offensive — also appears as entries 8 and 12 in this dataset."}
{"term":"тёлка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"tyolka","category":"insults","subcategory":"objectifying_term_woman","concept":"wench","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A girl or young woman (crude); literally 'heifer'; objectifying and mildly contemptuous but pervasive in colloquial Russian.","english_term":"chick","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Standard orthographic form (with ё); one of the most common crude-colloquial terms for a young woman in Russian; also appears as entries 7 and 12 in this dataset (simplified and repeated forms)."}
{"term":"мочалка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"mochalka","category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_object_woman","concept":"sexual_objectification","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":58,"recognition_pct_peak":62,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'washcloth or bath loofah'; prison and criminal argot for a woman regarded purely as a sexual use-object to be worn down through repeated use.","english_term":"piece of ass","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The washcloth metaphor is specifically apt: something used over and over until it deteriorates; more confined to criminal and prison environments than the other objectifying terms in this section."}
{"term":"давалка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"davalka","category":"insults","subcategory":"promiscuous_woman","concept":"sexual_permissiveness_pejorative","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A woman who puts out readily; derived from давать (to give), the sexual idiom meaning to be sexually available; implies a promiscuous woman who never refuses.","english_term":"easy lay","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Transparent derivation from давать ('to give/put out'); the -алка suffix is an agent-noun suffix turning the verb into 'the one who gives (sex)'; always pejorative."}
{"term":"подстилка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"podstilka","category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_object_woman","concept":"sexual_objectification","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'floor litter, bedding, or mat'; criminal argot for a woman who is laid down on by anyone — the image of a sexual doormat.","english_term":"doormat","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Evokes something placed on the floor for anyone to walk on or lie upon; harsher and more specifically dehumanizing than тёлка in its denotative imagery."}
{"term":"тёлка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"tyolka","category":"insults","subcategory":"objectifying_term_woman","concept":"wench","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A girl or young woman (crude); literally 'heifer'; objectifying and mildly contemptuous. Duplicate entry — see entries 7 and 8.","english_term":"chick","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Third occurrence of this word in the source dataset; entries 7, 8, and 12 are all the same word in differing orthographic conventions (е vs. ё) or as a repeated item."}
{"term":"мясо","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"myaso","category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_dehumanization","concept":"sexual_objectification","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'meat or flesh'; criminal argot that reduces women to raw sexual matter, the most extreme level of dehumanizing objectification.","english_term":"meat","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"мясо also circulates in gaming and internet contexts ('пушечное мясо' = cannon fodder), reinforcing its sense of disposable material; in the sexual context the reduction is total."}
{"term":"кадр","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"kadr","category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_target","concept":"sexual_objectification","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":58,"technical":8,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":73,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'frame/shot/cadre/personnel file'; criminal argot for a person — typically female — identified and marked as a candidate for sexual exploitation.","english_term":"mark","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"In general Russian slang кадр means 'what a character/specimen'; the criminal-argot overlay frames the person as a personnel file to be acted upon — selected, assessed, and used."}
{"term":"дедовщина сексуального характера","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"dedovshchina seksualnogo kharaktera","category":"acts","subcategory":"military_sexual_hazing","concept":"dedovshchina_sexual_hazing","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":75,"technical":28,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual abuse perpetrated within the дедовщина system — the institutionalized caste-based hazing hierarchy of the Soviet and Russian military — by senior conscripts against junior ones.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"Дедовщина (from дед, 'grandfather/old timer') is a Soviet and post-Soviet military institution in which senior conscripts systematically abuse juniors across a rigid caste ladder; the sexual component uses rape and coercion to establish dominance and silence reporting through homophobic shame. No English term captures both the institutional caste structure and the sexual violence dimension simultaneously."}
{"term":"духи","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"dukhi","category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"hazing_hierarchy_rank","concept":"military_hazing_victim_rank","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":40,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Plural of дух ('spirit/ghost'); the lowest caste in the дедовщина military hierarchy — first-year conscripts subjected to labor, humiliation, and sexual abuse by senior soldiers.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"Also used as a term for enemy fighters (Afghan mujahideen, Chechen combatants) in military slang. In дедовщина contexts духи are the primary sexual victims. The ghost metaphor implies they are not yet fully real soldiers — and therefore not entitled to human dignity."}
{"term":"дух","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"dukh","category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"hazing_hierarchy_rank","concept":"military_hazing_victim_rank","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":40,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Singular of духи; a single first-year conscript at the bottom of the дедовщина caste hierarchy, subject to sexual abuse and forced servitude by senior soldiers.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"Singular form of entry 16. Primary civilian meanings are 'spirit/soul' and 'scent/aroma'; the military hazing meaning is entirely register-specific."}
{"term":"салага","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"salaga","category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"hazing_hierarchy_rank","concept":"military_hazing_victim_rank","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":8,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A raw, inexperienced military recruit or sailor; in дедовщина contexts, a novice conscript at or near the bottom of the hazing caste and therefore exposed to sexual and physical abuse.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"Originally navy slang — likely from a small worthless fish; migrated across all service branches. Functions more as a general insult for inexperience than a formally fixed caste rank in the way дух/духи is; overlap with that concept is strong."}
{"term":"молодой","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"molodoy","category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"hazing_hierarchy_rank","concept":"military_hazing_intermediate_rank","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":25,"technical":8,"recognition_pct_current":83,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'young one'; in the дедовщина hierarchy, the second-year conscript rank — above духи but still subordinate to деды — both victim and perpetrator in the cycle of sexual hazing.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"The intermediate caste: молодые have survived their first year and are now entitled to victimize духи while remaining subject to the деды. This structural position perpetuates the cycle. No English concept captures the intermediate perpetrator-victim role in a military sexual-hazing caste hierarchy."}
{"term":"принудить","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"prinudit'","category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_coercion","concept":"ravishment","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":45,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To force or coerce; in дедовщина and criminal argot contexts, a euphemistic verb for compelling someone to perform a sexual act — i.e., rape or sexual coercion.","english_term":"to force","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The verb itself is neutral (to compel/force); the sexual meaning is entirely context-dependent. Used in дедовщина discourse as a distancing or legalistic euphemism for rape."}
{"term":"опустить","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"opustit'","category":"acts","subcategory":"prison_caste_rape","concept":"prison_rape_degradation_caste","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to lower or put down'; in Russian prison and criminal culture, to forcibly rape a man — typically anally — in order to permanently demote him to the опущенные caste, the irreversibly degraded stratum of the criminal hierarchy.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"One of the most culturally loaded concepts in Russian criminal culture. The act creates a permanent and irreversible caste change: the victim becomes опущенный ('lowered/degraded'), permanently untouchable and barred from normal social contact with other prisoners. No English concept captures both the specific act and the permanent social-caste consequence. The matching dедовщина usage transfers this prison logic into the military barracks context."}
{"term":"гомофобные оскорбления","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"gomofobnyye oskorbleniya","category":"insults","subcategory":"homophobic_slur","concept":"homosexual_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":78,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A descriptive or meta phrase for homophobic slurs used in дедовщина contexts to shame sexually abused junior soldiers and prevent them from reporting abuse.","english_term":"homophobic insults","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"A category label rather than a single slur; included in дедовщина sexual-hazing vocabulary because homophobic shaming is the primary silencing mechanism — perpetrators frame rape as making the victim gay, ensuring victims cannot report without identifying themselves as homosexual under Russia's hostile social and legal climate."}
{"term":"ёб твою мать","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"yob tvoyu mat'","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_imprecation","concept":"motherfucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"One of the most powerful Russian mat phrases; literally '(I/he) fucked your mother'; deployed as an expression of extreme rage, contempt, or emphasis.","english_term":"motherfucker","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Structurally parallel to English 'motherfucker' but second-person accusative ('your mother') rather than a compound noun. Part of core Russian мат — the highly restricted obscene register. Extremely pervasive in military speech; saying it to a superior can result in serious consequences; its frequency in barracks environments is near-constant."}
{"term":"материть","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"materit'","category":"insults","subcategory":"mat_profanity","concept":"mat_obscene_cursing","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_crude","crude":60,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To curse at or verbally abuse someone using мат — the Russian system of strongly obscene language — as a form of aggression, dominance, or humiliation.","english_term":"to curse someone out","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Мат is a discrete register of Russian built around a small set of root words (хуй, пизда, ёб/ебать, блядь, etc.) with specific social rules governing permissible contexts. Материть is the transitive form — to direct мат AT a person rather than merely using profanity in general. Pervasive in дедовщина as an ongoing instrument of dominance; no English verb captures both the specific register system and the directional-abuse function."}
